     <h1 class="title" title="Amboli Hill Station">Amboli</h1>
     <div class="entry-content">
<p>

<img src="https://storage.googleapis.com/createweb/INDIAHILLSTATION.INFO/images/west-india-hill-stations/amboli-hill-station.jpg" title="Amboli hill station" alt="Amboli hill station, hill stations in india, 

west india hill stations, Amboli" style="width:200px;height:150px" class="thumb alignright"/>


<b>Location:</b> Sindhudurg district,Maharashtra.<br />
<b>Significance:</b> Known as Cheerapunji of Maharashtra<br />
<b>Altitude:</b> 690m above sea level<br />
<b>Climate:</b> Summer 35&#176;C, Winter 12&#176;C<br />
<b>Best time to visit:</b> September to May</p>     
<p><b>Ambola</b> is a mountain resort in the grip of peace and tranquility. Located at an altitude of 690 m, Ambola is located in the <b>Sindhudurg district</b> of <b>Maharashtra</b>. This is the last mountain resort before the coastal plain of south are <b>Sahyadri hills</b>. On one side of the <b>Konkan coast</b> is Ambola, the other three, flanked by <b>beautiful valleys to see</b>. Ambola receives an annual rainfall of about 750 centimeters, making it the wettest place in Maharashtra. Due to heavy rains Ambola these steep hills is surrounded by dense bush. The view from the eyes of birds haunting the beach <b>Konkan hills</b> above Ambola attracts thousands of tourists here.</p>
